  <title>Count inventory</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Inventory</gui><gui>Count</gui></guiseq> records a stock
  count, product by product, into a count summary: one count of one location
  in one fiscal year. Several people can count into the same summary at
  once, on different computers.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the count summary in the box beside <gui>Inventory
    summaries</gui>. To start a new count, click <gui>Inventory
    summaries</gui> first; see <link xref="inventory_summaries"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Scan each item into <gui>Product barcode</gui>: each scan adds one
    to that product's <gui>Qty</gui>. Or choose a product under
    <gui>Product</gui> and type its quantity. Click a <gui>Qty</gui> to correct
    it.</p></item>
    <item><p>Barcodes that match no product are listed under <gui>Missing
    barcodes</gui>, with how many times each was scanned, to sort out
    later.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Below the list are the <gui>Total products :</gui> counted and their
  <gui>Total Cost :</gui> and <gui>Total Retail :</gui>. Right click a product
  to <gui>Delete</gui> it from the count or open its <gui>Product
  hub</gui>.</p>

  <section id="close">
  <title>Closing the count</title>
  <p>When everything is counted, click <gui>Close count</gui>. You are shown
  how many units were counted, against how many the books have at that
  location, and asked to confirm. Closing corrects the stock of every product
  counted to the quantity counted; a product already right is left alone.
  Any products that cannot be corrected are listed first and skipped.</p>
  <note><p>A closed count cannot be reopened or counted into again. If
  someone closes the count while you have it open, you are told.</p></note>
  </section>

